{
  "id": "Compound::DB00674 - Gene::1137",
  "verbalization": "Galantamine, a cholinesterase inhibitor, is implicated in the interaction with multiple acetylcholine receptor subunits through a series of mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Galantamine binds to Chrna5, Chrnb4, and Chrna6, all of which are involved in acetylcholine receptor activity. These receptors are part of the broader acetylcholine receptor family, and their participation in acetylcholine-related processes indicates a potential role in neurotransmission. The shared involvement of these receptors in acetylcholine receptor activity suggests a common biological function, which may be relevant to the therapeutic effects of Galantamine. The integration of these pathways implies that Galantamine may modulate acetylcholine receptor function through binding to different subunits, potentially influencing receptor activity and signaling. The observed scores indicate a consistent and significant relationship, though further validation with experimental data would be necessary to confirm the mechanistic relevance.",
